An original Zig implementation
------------------------------

The blob/blobmsg TLV codec (the bulk of the module) implements the OpenWRT
libubox wire format from its headers `blob.h`/`blobmsg.h` (**ISC**) as the
format specification — independent Zig implementation, no libubox code copied.

The ubus message envelope uses the 8-byte `msghdr` struct layout and the ubus
protocol constants (`MSG_*`/`ATTR_*`) as declared in ubus `ubusmsg.h`
(**LGPL-2.1**); these are uncopyrightable protocol facts (integer constants +
a packed struct), re-derivable from the documented header layout.

`libubus-io.c` (**LGPL-2.1**) contributed NO code: the unix-socket transport
(blocking read/write loops, single-buffer send, fixed-header framing,
seq-matched request/reply) is an independent implementation — none of
`libubus-io.c`'s expression (writev/iovec scatter-gather, chunked reader,
`SCM_RIGHTS` fd-passing, callback request-registry, reconnect state machine) is
present.

Published under MIT; the only copyleft touchpoint is the uncopyrightable ubus
protocol facts above.

Black-box test oracle
---------------------

A real ubusd integration test (connect, list, invoke) passes against a live
daemon when present. `codec.zig`'s "real ubusd capture" tests freeze wire bytes
and matching `ubus -S` JSON text from a real `ubus`/`ubusd` pair run once
inside the `scripts/vm/` OpenWRT VM, exercising it purely as a black-box test
oracle (root NOTICE §0 — no libubus/ubus source consulted, needing no
attribution beyond this record); see `SPEC.md` for the byte-parity findings.
